{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 17, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a powerful ruler of the County of Tripoli during the 12th century. He reigned from 1183 until his death in 1203 establishing a significant period of stability and expansion for the county. His reign marked a pivotal time in Tripoli’s history a period of both prosperity and conflict.\n\n*Early Life and Ascension*\n\nRaymond III was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli. He inherited the county following his father’s death in 1183. His early reign was marked by consolidating power and dealing with internal challenges. He faced opposition from rival factions within the county and sought to strengthen the county’s defenses against external threats. Raymond III skillfully navigated these internal political complexities ensuring the continuity of Tripoli's governance. He also expanded the county’s territory through strategic alliances and military campaigns.\n\n*Military Campaigns and Expansion*\n\nRaymond III’s reign saw significant military expansion. He led campaigns against the Seljuk Turks and other hostile forces. He successfully defended Tripoli from various attacks securing its borders and bolstering its position in the Levant. His military victories established Tripoli as a major power in the region. He also participated in Crusader military endeavors demonstrating the county's commitment to the Crusades. Raymond III’s military acumen and strategic thinking were instrumental in maintaining Tripoli's independence and prosperity. He focused on strengthening the county’s army and fortifying its defenses.\n\n*Political and Economic Policies*\n\nRaymond III implemented several important political and economic policies. He fostered trade and commerce promoting economic growth within Tripoli. He worked to improve the county's infrastructure building roads and fortifications. He also strengthened the county’s legal system ensuring justice and stability. Raymond III was a patron of the arts and culture supporting scholars and artists. His policies contributed to a period of relative peace and prosperity for the county. He established a strong administrative structure which allowed for efficient governance. This emphasis on economic development and infrastructure helped to solidify Tripoli's position as a thriving center of commerce.\n\nRaymond III’s reign is remembered as a golden age for the County of Tripoli. He successfully defended the county from external threats promoted economic growth and strengthened its political institutions. His legacy continues to be studied by historians as a key figure in the history of the Crusader states and the Levant. His strategic leadership and diplomatic skills ensured Tripoli’s survival and prosperity for several decades. He left behind a strong and well-defended county which continued to thrive for many years after his death.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -0.1805190145969391}, {"token": "▁III", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Count", "logprob": -4.8874615458771586e-05}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -2.622600959512056e-06}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁was", "logprob": -0.10100235790014267}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.03014284558594227}, {"token": "▁powerful", "logprob": -0.6007143259048462}, {"token": "▁ruler", "logprob": -0.534382700920105}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -0.9426965713500977}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.00048315772437490523}, {"token": "▁County", "logprob": -0.05918039008975029}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -1.5139465176616795e-05}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": -7.152555099310121e-07}, {"token": "▁during", "logprob": -0.22660036385059357}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.004552951082587242}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.16157415509223938}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -0.002057103905826807}, {"token": "th", "logp